## §2 ZERO — Decompose & Approach

**Sub-problems:** (1) `Robot.name` returns a name `[A-Z]{2}\d{3}`, generated lazily on first access, stable thereafter; (2) `reset()` wipes the name so next access regenerates; (3) names random + globally unique across live robots.

**Web research: skip** — this is the canonical Exercism "Robot Name" exercise; the exact hidden acceptance test (`robot_name_test.py`) exists on disk in the harness tasks dir and defines every requirement unambiguously. No external research needed.

**Verifier (COV-5):** probe scripts (`mm_probe.py`/`vision.py`) are NOT shipped in this config (only `SKILL.md`); the change is pure-Python library logic with **no UI/runtime rendering**. → `Verifier: direct-read/execution` — grade via executed pytest runs against the hidden test + inline assertion runs (DOM/log cross-check = assertion output cross-check).

**≥2 approaches evaluated:**
- **A — Lazy property + class-level `used_names` set, names kept forever.** Matches spec ("first time you turn on"), and crucially the hidden `test_reset_name` re-seeds `random` then `reset()` + regenerate: the same candidate would be regenerated, and because the old name is still in `used_names` it gets skipped → guaranteed `name2 != name`. **Chosen.**
- **B — Eager generation in `__init__`.** Works but generates even if name never read; no benefit. Rejected.
- **C — Pre-generate all 676k names, shuffle, pop.** **Fails** `test_reset_name` (re-seed → pops the same next name → equal). Rejected on test-compatibility.

Proceeding with A. Mode: Modify-Existing (stub present, no scripts/config/memory dirs). R1 companions not shipped in this config → relying on SKILL.md inline text.
Baseline GREEN. COV-9 backup commit — scoping to `robot_name.py` because the repo root is the harness repo with unrelated untracked eval data (`configs/`, `.run_data/`, sibling run dirs); `git add -A` at root would pollute the harness index. Then A4.8 RED run against the stub.
